{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":" is a domain plugin that owns the paywall slice of your app’s state and routes paywall actions through the Swidux dispatch cycle. It is provider-agnostic: the plugin knows nothing about RevenueCat, StoreKit, products, prices, or purchase results. You supply a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":" conformer that talks to whichever purchase backend you use, and the plugin manages presentation state, async progress, and entitlement transitions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For end-to-end wiring, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"reference"},{"text":". For where this plugin sits in the lifecycle, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Library-target","text":"Library target","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Product: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Import: ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the product to your target dependencies in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":" alongside ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Provided-implementations","text":"Provided implementations","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin ships with two in-repo conformers, both provider-agnostic and SDK-free:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"MockPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fixed snapshot, stream finishes immediately; for previews and tests.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SimulatedPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a stateful, fully driveable service. Paired with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" debug sheet, it lets a developer or QA tester grant Pro\/Trial\/Permanent, restore, and simulate failure\/latency — all flowing through the real plugin pipeline, with no SDK and no vendor commitment. Use it as the ","type":"text"},{"code":"service:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" while the paywall vendor decision is still open.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For production RevenueCat integrations, the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"reference"},{"text":" companion package provides:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"RevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer that bridges RevenueCat’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stream and ","type":"text"},{"code":"restorePurchases()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" API.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a RevenueCat-flavored mock for previews.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a SwiftUI sheet built on RevenueCatUI that hands purchase results back through the plugin.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Full API documentation lives in the package’s own ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For other backends (StoreKit, custom server), implement "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" directly — see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" Step 3, Path B."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Resilient-last-known-good-decorator","text":"Resilient last-known-good decorator","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResilientPaywallService"},{"text":" wraps any ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so a transient failure to read entitlements at cold launch never presents a previously-seen paid user as free. It retries with backoff, then falls back to a last-known-good snapshot persisted through an injected ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Because that cache vouches for a paid entitlement while offline, back it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — not ","type":"text"},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose plist a user can edit or restore from a doctored backup:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let resilient = ResilientPaywallService(","    base: paywallService,","    store: KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Feed the wrapped instance to both "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin(..., service:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and any app-side entitlement reader. The live provider stays authoritative: any successful snapshot overwrites the cache. See the type’s own documentation for the staleness policy and threat model."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Types","text":"Types","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"`PaywallPlugin<RootState, RootAction>`","anchor":"PaywallPlugin%3CRootState-RootAction%3E"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer. Owns a slice of root state typed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and an action enum typed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public init(","    state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, PaywallState>,","    action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (PaywallAction) -> RootAction,","    extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> PaywallAction?,","    service: any PaywallService,","    openURL: @escaping @Sendable (URL) async -> Void = { \/* default *\/ }",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"text":" handler calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIApplication.shared.open"},{"text":" on UIKit and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSWorkspace.shared.open"},{"text":" on AppKit. Override it for testing or for non-standard environments.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"PaywallState","level":3,"text":"`PaywallState`","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct. The slice the plugin owns.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct PaywallState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var isPro: Bool","    public var hasPermanentLicense: Bool","    public var isPresented: Bool","    public var requestedReason: String?","    public var isLoading: Bool","    public var error: String?","    public var isCustomerCenterPresented: Bool","    public var isObservingCustomerInfo: Bool","","    public init(","        isPro: Bool = false,","        hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false,","        isPresented: Bool = false,","        requestedReason: String? = nil,","        isLoading: Bool = false,","        error: String? = nil,","        isCustomerCenterPresented: Bool = false,","        isObservingCustomerInfo: Bool = false","    )","","    public var isGateSatisfied: Bool { isPro || hasPermanentLicense }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"isGateSatisfied","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the single read your feature code should consult before running gated work. It is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" when the user holds an active pro subscription or a permanent license.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"PaywallAction","level":3,"text":"`PaywallAction`"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public enum PaywallAction: Sendable {","    case request(reason: String)","    case dismiss","    case observeCustomerInfo","    case refreshCustomerInfo","    case customerInfoUpdated(EntitlementSnapshot)","    case refreshFailed(String)","    case restorePurchases","    case presentCustomerCenter","    case dismissCustomerCenter","    case openManageSubscriptions","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"EntitlementSnapshot","level":3,"text":"`EntitlementSnapshot`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Provider-agnostic value the service emits to describe the user’s current entitlement.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct EntitlementSnapshot: Sendable, Equatable {","    public let isPro: Bool","    public let hasPermanentLicense: Bool","","    public init(isPro: Bool = false, hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false)","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"PaywallService-protocol","level":3,"text":"`PaywallService` (protocol)"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol PaywallService: Sendable {","    func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"MockPaywallService","level":3,"text":"`MockPaywallService`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Test\/preview conformer that returns a fixed snapshot. Its stream finishes immediately.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct MockPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(isPro: Bool = false, hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false)","    public func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    public func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    public func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","}"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"`SimulatedPaywallService`","anchor":"SimulatedPaywallService"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Stateful ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actor"},{"text":" conformer for development and QA. Holds the current entitlement and multicasts changes through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoStream()"},{"text":", so simulated grants survive a later ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCustomerInfo"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases"},{"text":" exactly as a real service would.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public actor SimulatedPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(","        isPro: Bool = false,","        hasPermanentLicense: Bool = false,","        subsystem: String = \"Swidux\",","        category: String = \"Paywall\"","    )","","    \/\/ PaywallService: customerInfo \/ customerInfoStream \/ restorePurchases","","    \/\/ Simulation surface (not part of PaywallService — driven by the dev UI):","    public func grantPro()","    public func grantTrial()","    public func grantPermanentLicense()","    public func setFree()","    public func setRestoreShouldFail(_ shouldFail: Bool)","    public func setRefreshShouldFail(_ shouldFail: Bool)","    public func setArtificialDelay(_ delay: Duration)","}","","public enum SimulatedPaywallError: Error, Equatable {","    case restoreFailed","    case refreshFailed","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"text":" only models ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPro"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPermanentLicense"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grantTrial()"},{"text":" yields ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPro == true"},{"text":" and is distinguished from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grantPro()"},{"text":" only in the log line.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI","level":3,"text":"`SwiduxDevPaywallUI`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A separate, opt-in library product (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxDevPaywallUI"},{"text":") providing a bare-bones debug paywall sheet. It mirrors the shape of the vendor paywall UI so the call site is unchanged when a real provider is adopted:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["someView.devPaywall(","    state: store.paywall,","    service: simulatedPaywallService,","    onAction: { store.send(.paywall($0)) }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sheet shows the live "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState"},{"text":", grant buttons, real Restore\/Refresh flows, and QA failure\/latency toggles. On macOS the sheet uses a 400×600 minimum, matching the vendor paywall UI. Hold a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"single","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SimulatedPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance and pass it to both ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (as the plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"service:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and ","type":"text"},{"code":".devPaywall(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@State private var paywallService = SimulatedPaywallService()","@State private var store: AppStore","","init() {","    let service = SimulatedPaywallService()","    _paywallService = State(initialValue: service)","    _store = State(initialValue: .configured(paywallService: service))","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the one place a dev\/QA service is intentionally constructed outside ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because the debug UI must drive the same instance the plugin observes. Swapping to a real provider removes the shared-instance wiring and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxDevPaywallUI"},{"text":" import along with the two-line ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" change.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Action semantics","anchor":"Action-semantics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each case below describes the state mutation the plugin performs and the effect (if any) it returns.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"requestreason-String","text":"`request(reason: String)`","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPresented = true"},{"type":"text","text":" and stores "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"requestedReason"},{"type":"text","text":". Returns no effect. Dispatch this when a feature needs to gate behind a purchase."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"dismiss","text":"`dismiss`","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPresented = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"requestedReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Returns an effect that dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".refreshCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so the entitlement is reconciled after the sheet closes (the user may have purchased while the sheet was up).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"`observeCustomerInfo`","anchor":"observeCustomerInfo"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a long-lived effect that consumes "},{"code":"PaywallService.customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":" for every snapshot. Dispatch once on app launch (typically from a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".task"},{"type":"text","text":" on the root view). The effect lives for the duration of the stream. Idempotent: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isObservingCustomerInfo"},{"text":" guards against double-subscription, so a re-dispatched ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".task"},{"text":" (view identity change, scene reconnect) won’t start a duplicate stream.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"refreshCustomerInfo","text":"`refreshCustomerInfo`","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isLoading = true"},{"text":". Returns a one-shot effect that calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService.customerInfo()"},{"text":" and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"text":" on success or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshFailed"},{"text":" on error.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"customerInfoUpdatedEntitlementSnapshot","text":"`customerInfoUpdated(EntitlementSnapshot)`","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPro"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPermanentLicense"},{"text":" from the snapshot, clears ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isLoading"},{"text":", and clears ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"text":". Returns no effect. The plugin emits this internally; your code rarely dispatches it directly. Note that the plugin emits this on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" snapshot (each ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoStream()"},{"text":" value, every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCustomerInfo"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases"},{"text":"), not only on entitlement changes — observe ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallState"},{"text":" (or a value derived from it) for transitions rather than mapping this action directly. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"refreshFailedString","text":"`refreshFailed(String)`","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"text":" to the given message and clears ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isLoading"},{"text":". Returns no effect.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"restorePurchases","text":"`restorePurchases`","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isLoading = true"},{"text":". Returns a one-shot effect that calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService.restorePurchases()"},{"text":" and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"text":" on success or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshFailed"},{"text":" on error.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"presentCustomerCenter--dismissCustomerCenter","text":"`presentCustomerCenter` \/ `dismissCustomerCenter`","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Toggle ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCustomerCenterPresented"},{"text":". No effects. Bind these to a separate sheet if your purchase backend exposes a customer-center UI (RevenueCat does).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"openManageSubscriptions","text":"`openManageSubscriptions`","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns an effect that opens ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions"},{"text":" via the configured ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"text":" handler. This deep-links into the Settings → Subscriptions page on iOS and the equivalent on macOS.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Implementing-a-PaywallService","text":"Implementing a `PaywallService`","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin is purchase-agnostic. It does not know about products, prices, transactions, or vendor SDKs. Your conformer is responsible for translating whatever a backend reports into an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol has three methods:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — One-shot fetch of the current entitlement. The plugin calls this from ","type":"text"},{"code":".refreshCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Long-lived stream that yields every time the entitlement changes (purchase completes, subscription expires, family sharing update, etc.). The plugin consumes it from ","type":"text"},{"code":".observeCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Performs a restore against the user’s account and returns the resulting entitlement.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note what the protocol does ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" require: no product list, no purchase method, no receipt validation. Purchases happen inside whichever paywall UI you present (a RevenueCat paywall view, your own StoreKit-backed sheet, etc.). The plugin only cares about the entitlement that results.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A typical RevenueCat conformer holds a reference to the SDK and bridges its delegate or async APIs into ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"text":" values. A vanilla StoreKit conformer iterates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.currentEntitlements"},{"text":" and listens to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.updates"},{"text":". Either way, the plugin stays the same.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"generated":true,"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference"}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"title":"EntityStore","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Undo \/ Redo","role":"article","type":"topic","i